{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And You</b> — the sense of <b>Elohim of Hosts</b>: for You are the Elohim of hosts above in the heavens, and the Elohim of hosts below, who are Israel." "<b>Do not spare</b> — all traitors of wickedness, in whatever nation they may be."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 59, :notes {0 "Resolved 'טעם' as 'the sense of,' introducing his reading of the phrase.", 1 "The fragmentary Hebrew 'באי זה גוי יהיו' is rendered hyper-literally; it may be elliptical for 'be they in this nation or that.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:14.760402157Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}